QuickJS dependency correction

This package bundles quickjs-emscripten and quickjs-emscripten-core JavaScript
with the memory-view refresh correction from upstream PR #248:
https://github.com/justjake/quickjs-emscripten/pull/248

Base release: v0.32.0, df4efb9ef2cb25c417ecb57986da462d11b244ed
Correction: 28090bc15bce1862ade366a41d5d44bd34e6b525.
Distribution patch SHA256:
1197aa1f7726775408871721dd26bed1746f519e09b2fbdd1379dddffbe2a3de
The stock 0.32.0 WASM variants remain external dependencies.

The source-generated PNPM patch covers the published core's CommonJS/ESM
JavaScript and source maps. Bundling propagates the correction to installed
consumers of this package. A workspace install patch alone would not do so.
Remove this patch and its bundling requirement after upgrading to a released
SDK that passes the pending-job memory-growth and exhaustion regressions.

Reproduce the patch from an SDK checkout containing the correction commit and
an unmodified quickjs-emscripten-core 0.32.0 package directory:

  node scripts/generate-quickjs-patch.mjs <SDK checkout> <unpatched package>

The script verifies the original distribution checksums, uses the lockfile's
esbuild 0.25.9 through tsup, and reads the exact source commit without changing
the supplied checkout. Normal installs and builds do not fetch SDK source.

